sian equations $u=1$ and $u=2,$ and\n\n- two horizontal lines with Cartesian equations $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{4},$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/88d58291666ed60113e3d16c5bc30e6d4375cbae3501f8e3e26bd9bbacb4940d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b327bc4-3944-515e-8b78-f0dbcf55bc74" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Rectangular Preimage Given Its Image Under a Polar Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6311e30-21f7-5c5e-9328-735070425f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/c8662ff0f722b1c0b651bc35291242713ca57c271dc1011be75d2217e3f95f3c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326397} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b2f3fa-2bee-5922-914e-95a6284f5dda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/e6239ef3eb407b37db7029088b6671af710b38f81622735087205bfae0bde67f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326398} {:answer/id #uuid "33b961cf-db4f-5cfb-95fe-320579eddca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/ff3ef277236f696894e85fef3cd7c2cff227f5a1844628d5f34fb613644b43d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326399} {:answer/id #uuid "412b6db1-a753-5a88-9b81-22e8566b2047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/832658a3d3a6add5f39be27844d2df16a07576ac8578b03b69ebac784b5b4c61.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326400} {:answer/id #uuid "fd8affcd-4ee0-5